# Presentation-golden corpus manifest for Spyro 3 (fields as in
# scripts/presentation-corpus.manifest: name|start|interval|freeze|pins).
# The level loads by VBL ~841 under --skip-to-level and gameplay is live by
# ~1200; 1500 leaves the fade settled.
# The pin holds VBL 1500 on the sub-tick leg as well as the canonical one: the
# grid's intermediate samples land at +interval/2, so the pose the player walk
# was measured against had no __inter__ tile of its own.
# 2560 pins the camera inside the portal (VBLs 2544-2589), where the
# destination's preview picture fills the screen.
# 2700 pins the level transition past the grid's last sample: the movie's
# inputs end at 2589 and the run continues, so the sub-tick leg there is
# the transition gamestate, where the re-extract draws the cyclorama and the
# player and every other producer returns empty. The grid's own 2650
# intermediate sample covers the transition's start; 2700 covers it 50 VBLs
# further in, where the canonical frame no longer moves between ticks.
sunrise-spring-sunny-villa-portal-entry|1500|100||1500,2560,2700

# sunrise-spring-surface-swim arms the player draw's water-plane split.
# g_Spyro+0x28 is zero on every frame of the other three bk2s and of the whole
# 20k attract demo (six levels); it is non-zero from VBL 1889 to this movie's
# end, with animationState 0x2B (SWIM_MOVE_SURFACE) and movementState 0x0A
# (SWIM_SURFACE), so the split's classification, its depth cue and its cut have
# no other row in the corpus.
sunrise-spring-surface-swim|1900|150||1900,2000,2200

# icy-peak-reflective-mirror arms the player draw's mirrored copy.
# g_Spyro+0x2C is the avatar's height above a material-class-4 surface; of the
# 37 levels only Icy Peak, Midday Gardens, Frozen Altars and Bugbot Factory
# carry a class-4 material at all, and the word is zero on every frame of the
# other four bk2s and of the whole 20k attract demo. Icy Peak spawns beside
# such a surface: idle to VBL 1300, then Up + Circle (charge) with a 60-frame
# Right every 400 to hold the rink, and the word is non-zero from VBL 1858 to
# this movie's end, so the reflection's matrix negation, its inverted
# back-face test and its ordering bias have no other row in the corpus. The
# pins are the frames where the copy is least occluded by the surface above
# it: 5011 to 7167 pixels of the frame move when the reflection is suppressed,
# against 588 to 1421 on the grid samples after 2025.
icy-peak-reflective-mirror|1900|150||1900,1921,1950,1961,2000,2001

# sunrise-spring-camera-swing holds R2 from VBL 1500 so the camera orbits the
# player while two animated-kind mobys and the simple-kind gems, baskets and
# chest stay in view. The pins hold sub-tick presents mid-swing, where an
# animated record replayed in the tick camera's view space is displaced from
# the interpolated camera by half a tick of rotation.
# 1760 and 2000 pin the swing's distant-band poses, where the far world is HP
# geometry under --lod extended and the sub-tick re-extract has the most to
# lose. They cover the pose, not the sector-occlusion class itself: the
# occluder depth grid is a GPU readback and headless holds none, so a headless
# tile cannot see a cull verdict change. That class is measured windowed, per
# walk.
sunrise-spring-camera-swing|1500|100||1520,1540,1560,1760,2000

# 1500 pins the opening dialogue, complete and static from 1494: a large
# semi-transparent text box whose corners are semi-transparent textured quads.
# sheilas-alp-sheila-water-invisible: Sheila, the playable moby, turns invisible
# in the water at VBL 4556; that pin holds the present on both legs. The 4520 pin
# holds a sub-tick present while she moves through the world under a moving
# camera: her own motion must interpolate as her camera-relative motion does.
# 4494, 4498, 4508, 4512 and 4528 hold sub-tick presents while Sheila and the
# NPCs beside her blend into their next animations.
sheilas-alp-sheila-water-invisible|4400|100||1500,4494,4498,4508,4512,4520,4528,4556

# icy-peak-ice-crystal-destruction: an ice crystal shot at VBL ~1670 shatters on the
# PSX and its model stays on screen natively; the pins bracket the shatter.
icy-peak-ice-crystal-destruction|1500|100||1660,1674,1690
# title-demo: the plain boot with no movie; the title screen's rhynoc animates
# under a fixed camera. 510 pins the frame the jitter was reported at, on the
# canonical and the sub-tick leg alike. 2210 pins the present where particles
# streak on the intermediate leg: a primitive lerped from a previous-tick
# record that is not its own.
title-demo|500|20||510,2210

# open-options and open-atlas are the corpus rows for the 2D UI layer: they are
# the only movies whose frames carry its classes inside the visible band. At
# the pins open-options draws the options panel (3 semi-transparent POLY_F4,
# PSX box x 192..320 y 76..172), its 30 SPRT glyphs (x 208..308 y 80..152) and
# 5 HUD-class POLY_FT4 (x 128..384 y 65..193); open-atlas draws the whole atlas
# screen as 290 POLY_FT4 covering x 1..512 y 12..228. The in-game HUD sprites
# sit at y -28..2 — retracted above the visible band — on every frame of every
# other movie in this corpus, so no row shows the HUD extended yet.
# Both rows are freeze-marked. From VBL 869 the loading screen suppresses the
# framebuffer clear, and from VBL 1165 so does open-options' save prompt: the
# game draws no world and the last rendered frame is the backdrop of the 900
# pin on both movies and of open-options 1200 and 1300. That backdrop comes
# from the capture-time snapshot, which only a freeze-marked row maintains.
# open-atlas 1000, 1200 and 1300 sit on cleared frames and are byte-identical
# with the flag and without it.
# The atlas pages at 1200 and 1300 hold vertical seams between the page's
# POLY_FT4 tiles (a black column at 16:9 x 163 and fainter ones about 52 px
# apart, each ending in a black dot) that the PSX does not draw.
open-options|900|100|freeze|1200,1300
open-atlas|900|100|freeze|1200,1300

# open-atlas-turn-pages holds the atlas page-turn animation: the turning
# sheet is a skewed per-vertex-shaded quad (POLY_GT4) covering up to half the
# screen for 8 to 17 drawn ticks per turn, the only POLY_GT4 in the corpus.
# The pins bracket four turns: 1244/1252/1268/1276 (forward 1),
# 1320/1328/1344/1352 (forward 2), 1500/1510 (reverse 1) and 1524/1532
# (reverse 2), each a turning tick where the sheet covers the most screen.
open-atlas-turn-pages|1240|100|freeze|1244,1252,1268,1276,1320,1328,1344,1352,1500,1510,1524,1532

# title-demo-tracers: the attract demo's tracer ribbons, the only geometry the
# ribbon producer (func_8002FB68) emits anywhere in the corpus (VBL 4487-4535).
title-demo-tracers|4480|20||4501

# title-demo-glint2: the attract demo's jittered beams, the only geometry the
# ribbon producer (func_8002F5B4) emits anywhere in the corpus: the live byte
# at +0x1C of the eight records of D_80072430 reads zero on all six gameplay
# rows and on open-atlas, and one live record on the plain boot from VBL 4901
# to VBL 4922. The 4900 grid sample sits before that window, so the row carries
# its own negative.
title-demo-glint2|4900|10||4910
#
# crystal-islands-flame: a flame breath over the water in Crystal Islands with
# the HUD fully extended. The flame's primitives are written at VBL 1066-1090
# (peak 1078); 1080 is an intermediate leg inside the breath.
crystal-islands-flame|1060|200||1074,1078,1080,1086

# spikes-arena: the fight with Spike opens at ~VBL 4100. From 4120 the guest
# draws the boss health bar at the bottom right, a green-to-red gradient
# beside the boss icon; the pins 4140 and 4158 hold it on both legs.
spikes-arena|4100|100||4140,4158

# title-demo-camcut: the attract demo's third segment ends at VBL 5852 with the
# camera stepping 76110 world units in one tick, and every record the tick drew
# carries a previous tick of its own. The intermediate leg there shows the
# previous tick for the whole interval; the canonical leg is unaffected. Its own
# row rather than a pin on title-demo, whose 20-VBL grid would otherwise fan out
# over the 3600 VBLs between them.
title-demo-camcut|5800|100||5852
